{"id":"lifecycle-86372217487762526850","entity":"entity-46358977591869678499","noStates":"Policy definitions have no status field that the program writes or tests, so they have no states in the usual sense. What the code does keep is their condition on disk, and the download changes it. Before a download, the destination folder holds no definitions or older ones. A successful download replaces them, file by file, with the Microsoft package version: any existing file of the same name is deleted and the new one moved in. Nothing is rolled back if a move fails halfway. The folder is then left with a mix of old and new definition files, and the failure is only reported as a message naming the step that failed. Failure also leaves a scratch folder under the user's local application data behind, holding the partly unpacked package and possibly the downloaded installer file. That folder is removed only when every step succeeds. When the user is an administrator, the download also rewrites the destination folder's owner and permissions. After a successful download the user may choose to load the folder, and the program then saves it as the saved setting for the definitions source folder. Loading itself never changes a definition: a file either loads or is reported as a load error at that moment, and nothing about it is stored.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/DownloadAdmx.vb","firstLine":43,"lastLine":72},{"file":"PolicyPlus/DownloadAdmx.vb","firstLine":80,"lastLine":80},{"file":"PolicyPlus/DownloadAdmx.vb","firstLine":93,"lastLine":93},{"file":"PolicyPlus/DownloadAdmx.vb","firstLine":114,"lastLine":125},{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":758,"lastLine":762},{"file":"PolicyPlus/AdmxBundle.vb","firstLine":18,"lastLine":79}]}
{"id":"lifecycle-31121928221385551983","entity":"entity-54216265301484356956","stateFields":["Entries (a POL file's entries, read together: the value entry, its **del.<name> entry, the **deletevalues list and the key's **delvals / **delvals. marker)","RegFileKey.IsDeleter and RegFileValue.IsDeleter (a REG export)","registry value presence"],"states":[{"name":"Not configured","writtenAs":"no entry for the value: no registry value, no POL entry, no REG record. A new empty POL store (New PolFile) starts every setting here.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":99,"lastLine":104},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":365,"lastLine":373},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicyLoader.vb","firstLine":80,"lastLine":81},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicyLoader.vb","firstLine":95,"lastLine":100}]},{"name":"Configured","writtenAs":"a value entry with data and kind (SetValue). In a POL file it is a per-value state read beside the others: if a **del.<name> entry or a key marker is already in the file, SetValue leaves it there and the value entry, which sorts after **, wins when the file is read (WillDeleteValue 130-131).","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":105,"lastLine":109},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":118,"lastLine":135},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":374,"lastLine":382},{"file":"PolicyPlus/RegFile.vb","firstLine":226,"lastLine":236}]},{"name":"Queued for deletion","writtenAs":"POL file: an entry named **del.<value name> (DWord 32), or the value name listed in a **deletevalues entry (semicolon-separated). REG file: a value record with IsDeleter true. Never held in the registry, which deletes at once.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":92,"lastLine":98},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":118,"lastLine":135},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":157,"lastLine":159},{"file":"PolicyPlus/RegFile.vb","firstLine":240,"lastLine":247}]},{"name":"Key cleared","writtenAs":"A per-key state, covering every value under one key, unlike the per-value states above. POL file: an entry named **delvals. (or **delvals) in the key; a **deletekeys entry clears each listed subkey when applied. REG file: a key record with IsDeleter true. Never held in the registry. ClearKey on an already cleared POL key removes the marker with the values and adds it back, so it stays cleared.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":124,"lastLine":125},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":160,"lastLine":167},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":183,"lastLine":195},{"file":"PolicyPlus/RegFile.vb","firstLine":248,"lastLine":259}]}],"evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":14,"lastLine":24},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":118,"lastLine":135},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicySource.vb","firstLine":356,"lastLine":383},{"file":"PolicyPlus/RegFile.vb","firstLine":218,"lastLine":268},{"file":"PolicyPlus/PolicyLoader.vb","firstLine":117,"lastLine":147}]}
{"id":"lifecycle-50339469099680730133","entity":"entity-15432428091703108209","noStates":"A program setting is a named value that is overwritten in place; no record of it moves through stages that the program acts on. Two settings hold a one-time 0 to 1 marker (welcome download check done, advanced editor warning accepted), but these are separate preferences read as on/off, not a stage of the setting.","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/ConfigurationStorage.vb","firstLine":11,"lastLine":19},{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":48,"lastLine":49},{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":783,"lastLine":787}]}
{"id":"lifecycle-05497405005486126038","entity":"entity-01494854910295739228","stateFields":["Comments dictionary entry keyed by policy ID (UserComments / CompComments, CmtxFile.Comments); Nothing when the source has no comment file"],"states":[{"name":"Has a comment","writtenAs":"policy ID present as a key in the in-memory comment table with non-empty text; reaches the comment file only when the user chooses Save Policies","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditSetting.vb","firstLine":232,"lastLine":234},{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditSetting.vb","firstLine":281,"lastLine":281},{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":428,"lastLine":430}]},{"name":"No comment","writtenAs":"policy ID absent from the in-memory comment table (key removed when the text box is emptied; the file drops it only at the next Save Policies)","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditSetting.vb","firstLine":278,"lastLine":280},{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditSetting.vb","firstLine":235,"lastLine":237}]},{"name":"Comments unavailable","writtenAs":"comment table is Nothing for the policy source (no comment path, or loading threw); box disabled with 'Comments unavailable for this policy source', nothing written, nothing saved","evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":331,"lastLine":332},{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":341,"lastLine":343},{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditSetting.vb","firstLine":229,"lastLine":231},{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditSetting.vb","firstLine":277,"lastLine":277},{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":618,"lastLine":618}]}],"evidence":[{"file":"PolicyPlus/CmtxFile.vb","firstLine":2,"lastLine":6},{"file":"PolicyPlus/Main.vb","firstLine":348,"lastLine":349},{"file":"PolicyPlus/EditSetting.vb","firstLine":276,"lastLine":283}]}
